      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>Caribou is the largest city in Aroostook County, Maine — the northernmost county east of the Mississippi River. With a population of approximately 7,400, Caribou is the commercial hub of the central Aroostook region and serves as the access point for cannabis retail in the St. John Valley and northern Aroostook.</p>
    <p>Per the Weedmaps directory, Caribou has 5 cannabis dispensary locations as of mid-2026, making it one of the better-served small cities in Maine despite its distance from Portland and the southern Maine market. Adult-use retail is legal for 21+ customers, and several operators also serve medical patients with valid Maine MMMP cards.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why Caribou Is a Cannabis Cluster</h2>
    <p>Several factors make Caribou a meaningful Aroostook County cannabis market despite the small population:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Regional commercial center.</strong> Caribou is the commercial hub for central Aroostook County, with shoppers traveling from Presque Isle, Fort Fairfield, Limestone, and the surrounding towns.</li>
      <li><strong>St. John Valley access.</strong> Caribou is the southern anchor for the St. John Valley (Madawaska, Fort Kent, Van Buren), the large rural area north of Caribou along the Canadian border.</li>
      <li><strong>Canadian cross-border demand.</strong> Caribou sits on US Route 1, the main north-south corridor through Aroostook. New Brunswick residents with valid US travel documents can purchase Maine adult-use cannabis (though possession across the international border remains federally illegal for them).</li>
      <li><strong>Multiple operators.</strong> The cluster of 5 dispensaries suggests the market supports competition, which generally means better prices, more product variety, and stronger operator investment in customer service.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Dispensary Operators in Caribou</h2>
    <p>Per the Weedmaps and Leafbuyer directories, the main cannabis dispensary operators in Caribou include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Richardson Remedies</strong> — 9 Bog Road, Caribou. Adult-use and medical. Also operates a sister storefront in Presque Isle.</li>
      <li>Other operators in the Weedmaps and Leafbuyer directories — verify the current list and hours directly with each location.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Use the Weedmaps Caribou directory and the Leafbuyer Caribou listings to see the current full operator list, hours, and menus. The market rotates with new operators opening and existing operators expanding.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Service Area</h2>
    <p>Caribou dispensaries serve a large geographic area across central and northern Aroostook County:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Caribou</strong> (in town) — 5 min</li>
      <li><strong>Presque Isle</strong> — 15-20 min south on US Route 1</li>
      <li><strong>Fort Fairfield</strong> — 15 min east</li>
      <li><strong>Limestone</strong> — 20 min northeast (Loring Air Force Base area)</li>
      <li><strong>Washburn</strong> — 20 min southwest</li>
      <li><strong>Mapleton / Ashland</strong> — 25-35 min south</li>
      <li><strong>Van Buren</strong> — 30 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Madawaska</strong> — 45 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Fort Kent</strong> — 60 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Houlton</strong> (county seat) — 60 min south</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For residents of the St. John Valley (Madawaska, Fort Kent, Frenchville, Van Buren), Caribou is the closest major dispensary cluster. The next-closest options are in Houlton (60 min south) or across the border in New Brunswick.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Adult-Use vs Medical in Caribou</h2>
    <p>The Caribou market includes both adult-use and medical dispensary models. Per the Weedmaps directory:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Several Caribou operators are licensed for adult-use (21+) and serve walk-in adult customers with valid government-issued photo ID.</li>
      <li>Some Caribou operators also serve medical patients with valid Maine MMMP cards, often with medical-specific menu options and discounts.</li>
      <li>Both adult-use and medical products must pass Maine's OCP-licensed testing panel (CATLab, MCR Labs, Nelson Analytical, Nova Analytic Labs).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Confirm each dispensary's specific license framework, hours, and menu with the operator before visiting.</p>
  </section>

